'''Corpse Walk''' is a [[skill]] granted by {{il|Corpsewalker}}.

==Mechanics==
{{main|Desecrate#Skill functions and interactions}}

Corpse Walk spawns [[corpse]]s and/or [[Spectral Corpse]]s while [[moving]], one by one, on a time-based interval. It has a maximum of 12 corpses independent of other corpse generation skills. It spawns corpses with the same level as the area. 

It otherwise uses the same corpse mechanics as {{il|Desecrate}}. 

==Version history==
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.25.0|
* [[Corpse]]s spawned by the {{il|Desecrate}} and {{sl|Corpse Walk}} skills now have a flat 15% chance to match your spectres (or 100% in [[Hideout]] areas), rather than a 15% chance on top of being added to the main pool of corpse varieties that can be picked from. These [[Spectral Corpse]]s are now unusable for most purposes, and can only be used by [[Minion]] Skills such as {{il|Raise Spectre}} or {{il|Bone Offering}}.
** Spectral Corpses have a visual effect applied to them to help differentiate them from other corpses.
** Spectral Corpses can only spawn if you have the Raise Spectre Skill.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.17.0|
* Desecrate and Corpse Walk now have a static 15% chance to spawn a Spectre Corpse, rather than a 2x relative weighting compared to all other possible corpse types.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.12.4|
* Introduced to the game. 
}}
{{Version history table end}}

